# Test documentation

Every `[Fact]` / `[Theory]` method MUST have XML docs in this shape.
Analyzer enforcement is deferred; follow by convention and review.

## Template

Headings and body text are **English**. See `.cursor/rules/language.mdc`.

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// One-line intent: what behavior is guarded.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// Preconditions:
/// - ...
///
/// Steps:
/// - ...
///
/// Expected:
/// - ...
/// </remarks>
[Fact]
public void MethodName_Scenario_Expected()
{
}
```

## Rules

- Required on **all** Fact/Theory methods (no “too simple to document” exception).
- `[Theory]`: document once on the method; list cases / `InlineData` intent under Preconditions or Steps (do not duplicate per row unless a case is special).
- Do **not** invent custom XML tags (`<preconditions>`, `<expected>`, etc.).
- Keep remarks short; link to `docs/design.md` when the why is non-obvious.
- Method names stay descriptive (`Method_Scenario_Expected`); comments do not replace good names.

## Example

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// WriteAsync/ReadAsync round-trips a non-empty payload on a MemoryStream.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// Preconditions:
/// - Empty MemoryStream
/// - UTF-8 payload bytes
///
/// Steps:
/// - FrameIO.WriteAsync then seek to 0
/// - FrameIO.ReadAsync
///
/// Expected:
/// - Read bytes equal the original payload
/// </remarks>
```
